+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "The regression loads packages/agent/src/harness/runtime/drive/tools.ts with Node 24 TypeScript stripping and fakes only checkpoint IO, tool execution and outcome publication. Seven cases run: (1) persisted safe + current declaration safe + not cancelled replays (clear, invoke, effect, publish; non-error outcome); (2) persisted safe but declaration now \"never\" settles interrupted (read, publish; no clear/invoke); (3) persisted safe but tool missing settles interrupted without throwing; (4) persisted safe but declaration has no replay policy settles interrupted; (5) cancelled both-safe call settles interrupted; (6) persisted \"never\" with safe declaration settles interrupted; (7) missing tool consults only the checkpoint and publishes an isError outcome. Interrupted assertions also check toolCallId/toolName, terminate=false, preserved checkpoint text \"durable-progress\" and details {step:2}, and the interruption marker mentioning that the external outcome is unknown. Exit code is 0 on the repaired code (7 cases passed). Reverting the guard to the original `!cancelled && call.replay === \"safe\"` makes the script fail with AssertionError 'changed declaration (safe -> never): unexpected boundary calls' and exit 1, confirming it detects this stage's fault. Limitation: node_modules is not installed in this workspace and dependencies must not be installed, so the repository's vitest suites (for example packages/agent/test/harness/runtime/drive-tools.test.ts) and tsc typechecking could not be executed here; the focused standalone regression above was used instead."
+  }
+}
